The tera R package as a whole is distributed under the MIT license, as
described in LICENSE and DESCRIPTION. That license covers the R code and the
Rust glue code in src/rust, not the upstream Tera templating engine, which the
package wraps.

The templating engine itself is the Rust crate tera:

  Source: https://github.com/Keats/tera (crates.io: tera)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Vincent Prouillet
  License: MIT

The Rust crates that tera depends on are vendored at build time and carry their
own licenses, predominantly MIT and Apache-2.0. Authoritative copyright and
license statements for each of them are found in src/rust/vendor/<crate>, which
is shipped in the package sources as src/rust/vendor.tar.xz.
